The bundled derivative under python/memory_skill/ has been MODIFIED by the
dsh-memory-protocol contributors. Every file in that directory is a modified
version of the upstream source.

Summary of modifications
------------------------
1.  Memory model extended with fact cards (L1: facts / fact_history) and an
    evidence timeline (L2: fact_evidence) plus a cross-language alias index.
2.  Scope partitioning (world / web / platform / topic:<name> / file:<path> /
    session:<name>) with automatic scope bindings on write.
3.  Retrieval: fact-card precedence, meta-memory isolation (lesson / topic /
    context excluded from general search), question de-weighting restricted to
    strong alias hits, RRF leg weights adjusted (alias 3.5 / BM25 2.5 /
    semantic 0.5 / temporal 0.5) and a dedicated skill leg (weight 2.0).
4.  Protocol gate downgraded from hard denial to advisory reminders; weave no
    longer performs write side effects; turn ingestion split by role.
5.  MCP tool surface extended from 15 to 21 tools (fact cards, learning queue,
    pending review, episodes, channel toggle).
6.  Field-level AES-256-GCM encryption with GCM integrity reporting, plus
    key rotation and plaintext-to-ciphertext migration tooling.
7.  L3 retention policy (TTL + row cap) with L4 episode summaries, a trash
    table, and pruning that never silently drops evidence.
8.  Memory tree (branch x date x period), capability registry, persistent
    learning queue and pending-candidate store.
9.  Host integration layer for DeepSeek Harness: pre-step context injection,
    turn-stopping role-split ingestion, client component for the channel switch.
10. Machine-specific paths removed; all paths derive from DSH_HOME /
    MEMORY_SKILL_DB_PATH / MEMORY_MODEL_PATH environment variables.
11. Optional modules retained from upstream but not wired into the MCP surface:
    transparent proxy, web crawler, knowledge synthesis, room adapter.

